title: The Last Save Room (8-bit take)
tempo: 80

# An original piece written to match the *feel* measured from a reference track: ~80 bpm, dark and
# minor (G#m / E / B / F# and C#m), extremely bass-heavy (about half the energy under 100Hz) and
# dark overall, with almost nothing above 4kHz. It is not a transcription of the reference's melody.
# Uses the non-square voices: sine sub bass, FM bells and electric piano, organ pads.
#
# 61 bars: intro 6 | A 10 | B (loud) 8 | C (build) 16 | D (breakdown) 8 | E (loud) 8 | outro 5
# `bass` (sine) carries the quiet parts; `bass_hi` (FM, louder) takes over for the loud sections.

instrument lead:    @bell volume=0.3
instrument lead2:   @epiano volume=0.22
instrument arp:     @bell volume=0.12
instrument pluck:   @epiano volume=0.2
instrument pad_lo:  @organ volume=0.3
instrument pad_hi:  @organ volume=0.26
instrument bass:    @sine-sub volume=0.3
instrument bass_hi: @fm-bass volume=0.95 sub=0.15
instrument kick:    @noise-drums volume=0.7 echo=0
instrument snare:   @noise-drums volume=0.55
instrument hat:     @noise-drums volume=0.2 echo=0

